Michael Pease, Evan Wallace, Harvey Reed, Robert Martin, Vivian L. Martin and Steve Granata. Supply Chain Traceability Principles: A Manufacturing Meta-Framework, NIST IR 8536, final September 2026, DOI 10.6028/NIST.IR.8536. [Official publication](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/ir/8536/final) · [Complete 68-file-page report](https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/ir/2026/NIST.IR.8536.pdf).

Read the full report and examine its principles and data-linking mechanisms against one lot's changing custody, state and evidence. Distinguish authenticity of an information chain from accuracy of its measurements or suitability of its material. Compare selective disclosure with the evidence a receiving user actually needs.

The final PDF's title, author/citation page, contents and scope were inspected on 29 October 2026. The catalogue's shorter title and author list omit Robert Martin; use the actual final report's identity. The 2024/2025 drafts are distinct. Reference software keeps its own licence/version and was not executed here. Preserve government, collaborator, component and patent notices; no blanket CC coverage is asserted. This reading does not require a new Lince feature.

